          "text": "Apply M001 to the field k0 (a division ring), the finite-dimensional U0, Fin(n0), and uFamily. L1 gives dim U0=n0 and F004 gives independence, so this family's span is U0. F003 says every family vector is in W0, so closure under linear combinations gives W0=U0 in the nonzero branch. Discharge L2 and combine it with the zero branch of S002, obtaining W0={0} or W0=U0. Discharge L1 to the full implication, and universally quantify all the originally arbitrary data. This proves the asserted general irreducibility lemma, even if n0 has zero image in k0: there was no division by n0 or trace calculation.",
